    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This is a memory module with a few items mapped. Of course,
we have RAM, but we also have some other stuff, like a
terminal. We choose certain address ranges to correspond
to certain components, and we manage the reads and writes
to them.

To complicate things a little bit, we don&apos;t just need to be able
to read and write for loads and stores. We also need to be able
to read out instructions and support any accesses the debug
module needs to do. This is why we have three address inputs,
three data outputs, and three sets of control signals.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="2200" y="420"/>
    </visualElement>
